In article <1990Jun20.021328.19155@ariel.unm.edu> emullins@carina.unm.edu 
(Eric Mullins) writes:
>First, what are the odds of FINDING a wand of wishing on level 6?  I had
>always thought this was impossible, I guess not.

  You can find one anytime, but it's not very likely.

>
>After I got it, I followed some advice posted here several months ago and
>wished for:
>
>3 blessed scrolls of charging (I only got 1, why?)

  You don't always get as much as you wish for.

>wand of polymorph (I got it fine)
>
>It was then out of charges so I read the scroll of charging.
>then I wished for a blessed +2 war hammer named Mjollnir and got it.

  I believe using wishes to get weapons is wasteful.  You can get
all the weapons you need by sacrificing at altars (unless you happen
to be a neutral character, in which case you'll need a helm of opposite
alignment to help you out).  In the meantime you can generally create 
yourself an Excalibur if you need it.

>Now, I'm at a loss.  I assume there are 2 more charges + the last charge
>which will destroy the wand.  What wishing strategy is good for Pl8?

  If it were me, I would wish for:
    a blessed luckstone
    a gray dragon scale mail
    an amulet of life saving

  There are other reasonable choices, but you have a good chance of
getting them with the wand of polymorph, if you're patient enough to
use it right.

